<code>assert e != null => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(e.value);</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the key was previously in the map (i.e., `e != null`), then after the removal operation, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value associated with the key is also not present in the map (`!this.containsValue(e.value)`).
--------------------
<code>assert (e != null) => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(e.value);</code>

Explanation:
- `e != null` checks if the key was previously in the map.
- `!this.containsKey(key)` ensures that the key is no longer in the map after the removal.
- `!this.containsValue(e.value)` ensures that the value associated with the key is no longer in the map after the removal.
